                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_426">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        Balliol College (Domus de Balliolo). </orgName><p>‘iv (fly-leaf) has on
                        verso a 15th-cent. title Holcote super sententias. Nota Burnham [footnote:
                        ‘The same annotation is found in MSS 71, 212, 241, and 278; quod Burnham in
                        MS 114; Burnham in MS 311. This should be the hand of Richard B., who was
                        junior fellow of Balliol in 1414 (Emden i. 317).’] on 80 suggests that the
                        volume was at Balliol in the early years of that century, but there is no
                        donor’s inscription, and 24’ liber scribbled at the top of 1 is not in the
                        normal hand of the College inventory-marks.’ (Mynors, Balliol,
                     56)</p></provenance>
